  "period_note": "CONSOLIDATED (Group) basis, matching this bank's main Q4/annual series (see sources.json reporting_basis). Source: Southeast Bank's own BSEC-mandated 'Evaluation of the Quarterly Financials by the Audit Committee and by the Board' disclosure table, embedded in its annual report (a corporate-governance disclosure most banks answer with a checkbox, but which Southeast Bank answers with an actual Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4 balance-sheet-and-income-statement table for that report's own year, plus a comparative column for the prior year). Balance-sheet line items are the 1 January to 31 March 2024 period-end snapshot (basis reported). Income-statement line items and EPS are CUMULATIVE FROM 1 JANUARY 2024 (\"1 January to 31 March 2024\" exactly as the table's own column header states), not discrete-quarter figures -- flagged via the _cumulative suffix, basis reported, same convention as CITYBANK. Balance-sheet identity (Total assets = Total liabilities + Total equity + Non-controlling interest) holds to within BDT 1m rounding. Cumulative net profit after tax increases monotonically Q1->Q2->Q3 within 2024 (validated; no violation). Cross-checked against the FY2025 report's comparative column: all figures for Q1, Q2, Q3 and Q4 match exactly, no restatement found. This is the year of the sector-wide asset-quality recognition event already documented in this bank's own 2024_Q4.json (classified loans jumping to 54,813.65m, 14.82% NPL). The quarterly breakdown adds concrete detail: cumulative net profit built steadily through the year (922m Q1, 1,221m Q2, 1,570m Q3) before a severe swing to a full-year 433m -- implying a discrete Q4-alone LOSS of roughly 1,137m, the most severe of any quarter in this table's span, driven by a 4,217m Q4-alone loan-loss-provision charge (cumulative provision for loans rose from 5,631m at 9-month to 9,848m at year-end) -- the largest quarterly provisioning charge in the entire 2020-2025 recovered series.",
